//- Talent profiles (Name/Keywords/Requirements/Description) covering
//- Chapter 6's Common Talents (organized by skill), each archetype's own
//- talent list and specialization talent trees in Chapter 5 (Mystic/Sage/
//- Schemer/Scoundrel/Scout/Soldier and their specializations), the
//- Caste-granted talents, and the per-Culture talents. Too many to
//- hand-write inline like ccWeaponProfiles/ccArmorProfiles above, so this
//- loads from a JSON file instead (source/data/talents.json) via the
//- `require` local that generate.js's pugOptions exposes to every
//- template. An initial pass at this data (built from the PDF's text
//- layer alone) silently mismatched several specialization/culture
//- talents' names to the wrong descriptions, courtesy of the source PDF's
//- two-column layout - the final data here was instead transcribed
//- directly from the rendered page images to catch exactly that. A couple
//- of pairs of talents across different specializations share the same
//- name with different effects (e.g. "Scotopia" appears in both the
//- Robber and Hunter specializations) - those are disambiguated as
//- "NAME (SPECIALIZATION)" in this data/dropdown.
-
  const ccTalentProfiles = require('./source/data/talents.json');
  const ccTalentNames = Object.keys(ccTalentProfiles).sort();
